<title>AUSTRIA: Austrian Airlines to resume Tirana flights.</title>
<headline>Austrian Airlines to resume Tirana flights.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Airlines said on Friday it would resume scheduled flights to Tirana next Monday, March 24, ending a 10-day interruption to services.</p>
<p>In a statement Austrian Airlines said the first plane would arrive in the Albanian capital early on Monday afternoon.</p>
<p>Tirana's Rinasi airport reopened on Thursday when Albanian special forces succeeded in securing the area after days of unrest.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +43-1 531 12 254</p>
